{
    "background_story": "Joel was a skilled fisherman who spent most of his life on the water. He had a special affinity for catching fingerlings, the tiny fish that darted through the shallow waters of the lake. Joel's patience and gentle hands made him a master at handling these delicate creatures. As a young boy, he would spend hours observing the fingerlings, mesmerized by their iridescent scales and rapid movements. As he grew older, Joel began to study the art of aquaculture, learning how to breed and raise fingerlings in a sustainable way. He eventually started his own fish farm, where he cultivated a variety of species, always prioritizing the well-being of his tiny charges. Joel's love for fingerlings had not only brought him a successful career but also a deeper appreciation for the natural world.",
